ch as Chinese text, due to terminal encoding settings or limitations in terminal emulators, which can degrade user experience depending on the configuration. Despite potential issues with character display and intermittent connection failures—especially during critical operations—the protocol remains a robust, widely adopted standard for secure remote interaction in modern IT environments. Its reliability, broad compatibility, and strong security model continue to make it foundational for remote system access and management across diverse technological landscapes."}
